From a5979d7fbddb0d33bf3aabee9186c9dae4349d25 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ahnaf <ahnaf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:11:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Add HDR text for the focused pane

Builds on the HDR cursor. A new per-profile setting (Profiles > Colors,
with light/dark variants like the HDR cursor) draws the focused pane's
text brighter than reference white on displays with EDR headroom.

- The fp16 framebuffer and EDR engager now turn on for HDR text as well
  as the HDR cursor.
- The per-frame state computes a gain only for the focused pane (key
  window and active session), over a dark default background, when the
  display has headroom, and not while Night Shift is on (advanced
  setting hdrTextOffDuringNightShift, default on).
- The monochrome text fragment shaders apply the gain in linear light and
  scale the whole color down if a channel would exceed headroom, so hues
  are preserved. The cursor cell and emoji are not boosted.
- EDR is only held for HDR text while the Metal renderer is in use.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TFt6v6wHS1u3NS1UtAyQpr
